# LoBBS command IoC

LoBBS is a stateless slash CLI over mesh DMs. **Plugins own verbs and filter lines.** The registry peels one verb and runs the bus. One wireup file lists plugins.

Player docs: [README.md](../../README.md). Bus behavior: [docs/lobbs-commands.md](../../docs/lobbs-commands.md).

## Required layout

| Layer | Role | May include |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `LoBBSDispatch.cpp` | Trim line, session/auth lookup, `lobbsCommandsHandle` | `LoBBSCommandRegistry.h`, `AuthDal` for session only |
| `LoBBSHooks.*` | `lobbsAddAction`, `lobbsAddFilter`, `lobbsDoAction`, `lobbsApplyFilter` | No plugin or DAL headers |
| `LoBBSCommandRegistry.*` | Peel `/[id] verb`, arg cursor, pager, reply helpers, `lobbsDispatchSub`, `lobbsHelpForTable` | `LoBBSHooks.h` only (no `apps/*Commands.h`) |
| `LoBBSWireup.cpp` | `lobbsHooksReset()`, `lobbsMsgRegisterDisplay()`, each `lobbs*RegisterCommands()` | All plugin `*Commands.h`, `MsgCommon.h` |
| `apps/<App>/*Commands.*` | `slash_cmd` handler + filter callbacks | That app's DAL, `LoBBSHooks`, registry helpers |
| `apps/Msg/MsgCommon.*` | `lobbsMsgShiftIndex`, shared `display_human` for mail/news | Mail/News record field ids |
| `apps/AppUtil.*` | Core auth directory (load user, username lookup) | Auth DAL internally |
| `apps/<App>/<App>.cpp` | Construct app / DAL wiring | No command switch |

## Session and core auth

- `LoBBSSession` on `LoBBSCommandCtx` (`nodeId`, `userUuid`, `username`, `isSysop`). Dispatch resolves it once via Auth.
- Registry helpers: `lobbsCtxLoggedIn`, `lobbsCtxIsSysop`, `lobbsCtxUserUuid`, `lobbsCtxUsername`, `lobbsCommandRequireLogin`, `lobbsCommandRequireSysop`.
- Feature plugins must not `#include` `AuthDal.h`. Use session + `AppUtil`.

## Actions

- **`slash_cmd`**: `lobbsDoAction("slash_cmd", ctx, args)`. Every subscriber runs; compare `verb` and return silently if not yours. No claim flag. No central unknown-command reply.
- Dispatch sets `ctx.rest` to the mutable remainder; handlers use `lobbsArgShift`, `lobbsArgRest`, `lobbsArgShiftMany`, and `lobbsArgShiftUint` / `lobbsArgPeekIsUint` (full-token decimal, no `atoi` partial parse).
- Subcommand apps: `LoBBSVerb` table + `lobbsDispatchSub` (see Mail). Flags: `LOBBS_V_LOGIN`, `LOBBS_V_SYSOP`. `fn == nullptr` rows are help-only (dispatch skips them).

## Filters

- **`help_topics`**: append catalog rows for `/help` (title + short description). Help plugin seeds `help`, `hi`, `pN`.
- **`help_for_topic`**: query in `args` `LODB_F_TITLE`; set `value` `LODB_F_DESCRIPTION` when matched. Use `lobbsHelpForTable` on the same `LoBBSVerb` table as dispatch.
- **`status_lines`**: append one line each; `/status` pages the vector.
- **`display_human`**: mail/news list and read formatting live in `MsgCommon` (single registration from wireup).

Priority constants: `LOBBS_HOOK_PRIORITY_*` in `LoBBSHooks.h`. Hooks insert in priority order at register time.

## Do

- Help plugin owns `/help` and `/hi`. Status owns `/status` only. Time plugin owns `/time`.
- `/time`: show clock; sysop passes Unix seconds to set RTC via `perhapsSetRTC(..., forceUpdate=true)`.
- Auth: `/login`, `/logout`, `/whoami`, `/passwd`, `/users` subs in Auth plugin.
- Fs verbs are top-level (`ls`, `cat`, …) with sysop gate inside handlers.
- Call `lobbsWireup()` once from `LoBBSModule` construction.
- Use `lobbsRecordPush` for status/help line records. Use `LoDb::upsert` for idempotent saves in DALs.

## Don't

- Central verb switch or capped hook tables.
- `#include` plugin headers from `LoBBSCommandRegistry.cpp` or `LoBBSHooks.cpp`.
- Pre-tokenize the full line into `argv` (breaks multi-word mail/news bodies).
- Per-plugin `display_human` for mail/news (use `MsgCommon`).
- Eager insert of wall/yarn defaults on load miss (defaults in memory only until save).

## New plugin checklist

1. `lobbsAddAction("slash_cmd", …)` with verb compare + arg cursor.
2. Filters: `help_topics`, `help_for_topic`, `status_lines` as needed.
3. One `lobbsXRegisterCommands()` in `LoBBSWireup.cpp`.
